## 4. Proposed split of R5

### 4.1 Who is allowed to do each part
✓ = allowed · ✗ = ruled out by the guide · ⚠ = allowed, but not advised (reason given) · – = no capacity (T1)

| | R5a Harness | R5b Judge | R5c Held-out | R5d Red team | R5e Results |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Anurag (R1) | – | – | – (and R1 checks R5c, G4) | – | – |
| Aman (R2) | ✓ | ⚠ the judge checks whether retrieved passages support the answer, which is Aman's retrieval | ✗ tunes retrieval, which is part of the agent (G2) | ✓ builds no defences | ✓ (dev runs) |
| Jilesh (R3) | ⚠ the harness measures the agents Jilesh builds and tunes | ⚠ the judge grades the agents Jilesh builds | ✗ tunes the agent (G2) | ⚠ the agents' prompts are the first barrier against answer extraction | ✓ (dev runs) |
| Abhishek (R4) | ⚠ the harness measures attack success against R4's defences | ⚠ the judge grades answer leaks, which R4's output filter is meant to stop | ⚠ the numeric questions test the calculator Abhishek builds | ✗ builds the defences (G3) | ⚠ interprets E2, which measures R4's defences |
| Vidhya (R6) | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ doesn't tune the agent | ✗ the web-app login that stops "I'm the teacher…" is a defence (G3) | ✓ |

**Result:** none of R5 sits cleanly with Abhishek, so Abhishek takes no part of R5.

### 4.2 Proposal

| Part | Proposed owner | Why |
|---|---|---|
| **R5a Harness** | **Aman** | Allowed, and the same style of pipeline as the retrieval evaluation already in the repo |
| **R5b Judge calibration** | **Vidhya** | The only person whose own work the judge doesn't grade. The rubric and the teacher's labels sit naturally with the held-out cases (R5c) |
| **R5c Held-out cases** | **Vidhya** | The only person who is both allowed and available. Anurag checks the cases (G4). It is early work, which fits because most R6 work comes after L16 |
| **R5d Red team + E2** | **Aman** | Builds no defences (G3) and knows the data path, which helps with poisoned-passage attacks |
| **R5e Results** | **Vidhya** (final held-out runs, experiment log, results write-up) with **Aman** (dev runs and tables) | Whoever owns the held-out set triggers the held-out runs, and only after the playbook freeze (G6) |

